Require explicit round-trip capability metadata on every language, select each round-trip corpus from that metadata, and opt 45 audited backends into the signed 64-bit boundary, interpolation-sensitive string, control-character, and embedded-NUL groups their toolchains verified. The audit also fixed Crystal's embedded-NUL escape (now the JSON-safe ``\u0000``) and D's ``long.min`` literal, which previously wrapped to a positive value.
